### Auth API test requests
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Click "Send Request" above each ### block. Run the dev server first: npm run dev
###
### The extension keeps cookies automatically within this file, so running
### Register (or Login) once and then the requests below it in order will
### stay logged in as that same user - no manual cookie copying needed.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "name": "Test User"
}

### 2. Register with a role field in the body - should still come back as "role": "USER"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sneaky@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "isAdmin": true
}

### 3. Register again with the same email - expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

### 4. Login as the user from step 1
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

### 5. Login with the wrong password - expect 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "totally-wrong-password"
}

### 6. Login with an email that doesn't exist - expect the SAME 401 message as step 5
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody-here@example.com",
  "password": "whatever-password"
}

### 7. Missing Content-Type header - expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

### 8. Who am I? (run this right after step 1 or 4 to be logged in)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 9. Refresh the access token (rotates the refresh token too)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

### 10. Confirm /me still works after refresh
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 11. Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

### 12. /me should now be 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 13. Refresh after logout should also be 401 "Invalid refresh token"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

###
### --- Admin login ---
### Use the ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD you put in .env when you ran `npm run db:seed`.
### There is no separate admin endpoint - same /login as everyone else.

### 14. Login as admin (fill in your real admin email/password first)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "your-admin-password"
}

### 15. Confirm the role
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
